TextureDentHiCar @0x43ba70 / TextureDentMidCar @0x43c05c: the two 20-byte dent-uv
parameter blocks live at ebp-0x58 and ebp-0x40 in the original frame and are passed
BY ADDRESS to FUN_0043c700/FUN_0043c868, which read them as structs:
  +0x0c  new/old tpage   (asm 0x43bac1: mov %ax,-0x34(%ebp) = -0x40+0xc)
  +0x12  u               (asm 0x43bacb: mov %al,-0x2e(%ebp) = -0x40+0x12)
  +0x13  v
Ghidra split each block into scattered locals (local_5c[12]+local_50+local_4a+local_49
and local_44[12]+local_38+local_32+local_31).  gcc and clang order the reconstructed
stack slots differently, so the callees' +0x12/+0x13 reads hit the WRONG local on both
targets -- and DIFFERENT wrong bytes per target: the applied dent-uv delta measured
-66 on native and +116 on wasm instead of the dent-table value.  Effect: the car
damage-texture uv rewrite diverged native vs wasm at the first collision of the L9
attract race (cf56), the first nat<->wasm framebuffer split (cf59+, blob x=473..500
y=251..311).  Scattered-locals class (cf. patches 585/595).  Fix: one contiguous
20-byte array per block, field access via offsets, register-for-register with the asm.

